  "independent_scope": "Whole native selected-source content on both mattes, all9 selected poses plus adopted neutral at inherited maximum body reference 430.000000px across5both-matte pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipe rows actually viewed. Historical unselected sheet cells are not accepted by viewing their whole source. Physical UI zoom/density and real-time/interpolated/MP4 output not measured.",
  "observations": "Actually inspected the whole selected core source and three fresh selected singles on both native mattes, all 9 selected poses plus exact adopted neutral at inherited 430 px across 5 both-matte pages, and all 7 decoded discrete recipes. Gray round broad head, paired small pink-inner ears, dark cheek bands and crown spots, cream ruff/chest/belly, white eye surrounds with brown pupils, paired rounded dark-ended forepaws/feet and one thick banded side tail remain consistent. Fresh blink closely preserves usual crown/chin/torso/foot layout; no former head drop was seen. Greeting and left/right presentations have connected correctly directed arms and gaze. Think uses its existing paw near chin; aha lifts one compact rounded paw without a new digit. Fresh cheer has both arms raised and retains clean torso edges with no old ochre line stain on lower left. Species_a uses viewer-left paw at cheek and fresh species_b keeps the same paw near cheek/ear, avoiding an unexplained arm switch. Other sheet gestures retain small approximately 6–12 px head/ear contour variations at 430 px noted by producer, which read as hand-drawn active pose changes rather than major stretch or identity loss. Contours, eyes, markings and tail bands are clear at 430 px, including the original core's modest 1.112x enlargement. No fused facial lines, dirty blocks, stray alpha field, clipping, duplicate limb/tail or detached connection was seen. Native whole-sheet history contains unselected old blink/cheer/species_b, which this review does not accept. Discrete return states retain the exact adopted neutral.",
  "cautions": [
    "The core's active gestures retain small head/ear-height drawing variation. This is not a claim of pixel-identical outlines or continuous-motion approval.",
    "Real-time playback, interpolation, final MP4 and physical UI zoom/density remain outside the inspected native/max/discrete scope."
